{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too","id":1222772,"title":"I hate Melee Specialties (and you should too)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-28T18:40:30-07:00","id":1222772,"title":"I hate Melee Specialties (and you should too)","content":"Provocative title out of the way, I hate the way Melee Specialties are boring flat bonuses. Lets posit a few statements first:<br /> <br /> 1- Only one specialty applies at a time (Melee: Swords and Melee: While Mounted only give 1 die if using a sword while mounted) <br /> <br /> 2- Melee: Sword/Axe/Knife/Etc is rules legal. <br /> <br /> 3- Players usually stick to a single weapon type. <br /> 3a- players usually stick to a specific weapon, period.<br /> 3b- unlike action games, there's little incentive to switch between two different melee weapons. <br /> <br /> 4- Martial Arts, Thrown, and Archery, have basically the same problem. <br /> <br /> So here we are, a perfect recipe for bland specialties. The book says that specialties shouldn't always apply, but then allows players to specialize in a weapon they will have on hand 99% of the time. I made some example Solars/NPCs to help my players, a Crafter, a Martial Arts Hating Crusader, and a Kaiju Hunter. The Crafter has Melee: Weapons I Made, the Crusader has Melee: Opponents in a Form Charm ** and the Kaiju Hunter has Melee: Legendary Size Beasts**. For the crafter, i specifically wanted to buck the &quot;use one weapon only&quot; trend, so that was a nice specialty. Useful, flavorful, but still almost always applies. <br /> <br /> The Kaiju hunter though? Bullshit. Its a &quot;bad&quot; (in this case meaning &quot;mechanically sub optimal&quot;) specialty. There's no reason not to take Melee: Great Axes or the like, which will apply all the time. Same with the Crusader who hates Martial Artists. She'd be better off with Melee: Weapontype <i>in every conceivable scenario </i>. <br /> <br /> If we look at noncombat skills, they are more interesting. Medicine: Treating Poison is cool, but it'd be insane to allow Medicine: Using my Healer's Kit. Lore: Realm is a good choice, but not Lore: Referencing A Book. <br /> <br /> It can get bad with Ride and Sail too. Ride:Horses (or Ride:Familiar) is never going to not cover you unless the ST forces you to ride some other mount <i>specifically to negate your specialty</i>. I have never once been in a situation like that. <br /> <br /> So back to combat, what do we do? How do we reward Interesting specialties without punishing them for not being &quot;bland but optimal&quot;? First, let's skip the argument that Bland But Optimal isn't a problem and Players Should Just Do What Fits Their Characters, Man. We are here to rectify a problem. I have a few ideas. <br /> <br /> 1) remove Melee: Weapon Type or Melee: My Personal Artifact as valid. This would be a bad fix and personally hurt all of the &quot;ancestral weapon&quot; type players and &quot;ultimate katana master&quot; types. <br /> <br /> 2- allow a 2nd specialty. So we have Melee: Flycutter Yari AND Melee: Fae when using the Artifact Spear against a Fae, double dipping. I'm not sure how the math checks out on that. <br /> <br /> 3- devise a broad vs deep bonus system. The Flaws merit rightly only gives you a bonus when you suffer for it to prevent MinMaxing cheese. Melee Specialties should do likewise. Melee:Weapon is 1 dice, Melee: Opponent or Condition is 2, and Melee: Niche Backstory Thing is 3. <br /> <br /> Oh, and I don't know where to fit this in, but Disarm Gambits are NOT a solution to the Specialty Problem, because either A- you don't have a back up weapon, or B- your back up is a crappy dagger and not a Glorious Golden Surfboard On A Hilt. Neither scenario would make me think &quot;Oh great, my specialty for this opponent type outweighs the need to get back my actually useful weapon&quot;. Oh, and C- Call the Blade negates that strategy entirely. <br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":".  Clarified a few examples. 05-29-2018, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:33:03-07:00","id":1222787,"title":"","content":"Well cases where I think the specialty is too broad then I just exercise ST veto rights. Like &quot;big creatures&quot; is too broad in my opinion because it potentially covers everything from the horse size up. I mean one thing if the player said &quot;gargantuan creatures&quot; that refers to a specific merit and makes sense for the character. In a stance feels a bit broad since it sounds like it can be easily spread from just enabling the player an advantage against martial artists, which seems to be their goal, to applying to anyone who's actually learned how to fight. &quot;Oh they're fighting defensively? So that means they're in a defensive stance and I get my bonus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just tell your players you dislike it when they pick a specialty that they can apply almost all the time. I mean some of those feel like a broad version of a specialty that makes perfect sense for the character. &quot;I fight martial artists, so I've studied the weakness in the forms they go into and since its uncommon for a martial artist, who isn't an exalt, to master multiple forms I tend to not have to worry about them swapping out on me.&quot; Part of the problem you're dealing with is that the book does say specialties can be rather specific like a lore specialty in haiku, or a broad specialty like melee with swords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 05-28-2018, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:40:52-07:00","id":1222790,"title":"","content":"I mean...I'd just go for 1 in my games.<br /> <br /> I like my specialities to say something about my character. Less Melee &quot;Swords,&quot; and more Melee &quot;Close Quarters Fighting&quot; or Melee &quot;Multiple Opponents&quot; or Melee &quot;Shocking Brutality.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like...they should be useful a lot of the time, but any specialty that's going to ALWAYS apply is one I probably wouldn't let a PC use in my game. Instead of Ride (Horses) or even Ride (My Godblooded Familiar Horse), I'd go with Ride (Races) or Ride (Mounted Acrobatic Tricks) or Ride (Herding).<br /> <br /> Specialties should tell you about a character's nature and backstory...and they should mechanically encourage a PC to try to use tactics that make sense given that nature and backstory. A Dawn who grew up with the Marukani doing the whole cowboy thing who has a Ride specialty in Herding is going to try and use that specialty, so he'll make use of his experience to try and herd enemies the way he did cattle-might even take the same specialty in War to double down. A former pirate with lots of experience fighting below decks with the Close Quarters Fighting specialty has a motivation to try and drag the fight into close quarters to get that bonus die.<br /> <br /> So yeah, narrow specialties are good for the game. They should be something the PC knows in-character they're good at and tries to arrange to be able to use.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:55:42-07:00","id":1222792,"title":"","content":"I think you referenced the right answer and then side-stepped it. Treat situations where a player chooses to not use, or can't use, a speciality as applicable for the Flaw bonus. You don't mess with the dice math, and they get a benny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T20:40:43-07:00","id":1222811,"title":"","content":"I agree that the speciality in a weapon type is far to common a choice for players and does not add interesting flavour to the character like other specialities can. However I think you are exaggerating the circumstances to far. If you are heavily invested in Evocations for a single artifact weapon then sure you will always do your best to be using that weapon. However outside of that weapon tags can play a big role. Also you may not want to pull out your surfboard in every fight due to discretion.<br /> <br /> Know you're going to fight a crane style martial artist? Bring a flexible weapon to ignore his full defence. Mounted Opponent? Go for Reaching tag. Opponent in heavy armour who has neglected dodge so is terrible at standing up? Go for grappling or smashing to get him on the ground. The situational bonuses from the right tag do outweigh a simple +1 from a speciality. Yes many players may choose to ignore these factors, but that can likely be attributed to a Solar just being so powerful that they break the system.<br /> <br /> Disarming is still a factor. Comparing a mundane disarm attempt vs a charm based counter seems silly. If we compare disarm charms vs Call The Blade then disarming is definitely still valid. Charms such as Iron Wolves' Grasp, Fallen Weapon Deflection(depending on ST ruling on order of application), and Table Turning reversal can prevent Call The Blade from working. Mountain-Burden Stone also works, or any other custom magic or evocations people can come up with. Also the dagger isn't &quot;crappy&quot; unless compared to evocation investment. Loss of a speciality &amp; +1 attack/+3 dmg on withering attacks is not huge and may be the preferred option compared to the difficulty of retrieving your weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T21:12:56-07:00","id":1222819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222787#post1222787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well cases where I think the specialty is too broad then I just exercise ST veto rights. Like &amp;quot;big creatures&amp;quot; is too broad in my opinion because it potentially covers everything from the horse size up. I mean one thing if the player said &amp;quot;gargantuan creatures&amp;quot; that refers to a specific merit and makes sense for the character. In a stance feels a bit broad since it sounds like it can be easily spread from just enabling the player an advantage against martial artists, which seems to be their goal, to applying to anyone who's actually learned how to fight. &amp;quot;Oh they're fighting defensively? So that means they're in a defensive stance and I get my bonus.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Just tell your players you dislike it when they pick a specialty that they can apply almost all the time. I mean some of those feel like a broad version of a specialty that makes perfect sense for the character. &amp;quot;I fight martial artists, so I've studied the weakness in the forms they go into and since its uncommon for a martial artist, who isn't an exalt, to master multiple forms I tend to not have to worry about them swapping out on me.&amp;quot; Part of the problem you're dealing with is that the book does say specialties can be rather specific like a lore specialty in haiku, or a broad specialty like melee with swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Crusader's specialty is specifically people in a Martial Arts Form Charm. I refer to those as stances a lot, I forgot to use the proper term. <br /> <br /> Afaik there isn't a game term for &quot;Mini Kaiju&quot; like DnD has for size catagories. Large Beasts (or Legendary Size Monsters) seems to broad to you, but do you actually veto the rules-sanctioned Melee: Swords at your table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T21:23:08-07:00","id":1222821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222811#post1222811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the speciality in a weapon type is far to common a choice for players and does not add interesting flavour to the character like other specialities can. However I think you are exaggerating the circumstances to far. If you are heavily invested in Evocations for a single artifact weapon then sure you will always do your best to be using that weapon. However outside of that weapon tags can play a big role. Also you may not want to pull out your surfboard in every fight due to discretion.<br /> <br /> Know you're going to fight a crane style martial artist? Bring a flexible weapon to ignore his full defence. Mounted Opponent? Go for Reaching tag. Opponent in heavy armour who has neglected dodge so is terrible at standing up? Go for grappling or smashing to get him on the ground. The situational bonuses from the right tag do outweigh a simple +1 from a speciality. Yes many players may choose to ignore these factors, but that can likely be attributed to a Solar just being so powerful that they break the system.<br /> <br /> Disarming is still a factor. Comparing a mundane disarm attempt vs a charm based counter seems silly. If we compare disarm charms vs Call The Blade then disarming is definitely still valid. Charms such as Iron Wolves' Grasp, Fallen Weapon Deflection(depending on ST ruling on order of application), and Table Turning reversal can prevent Call The Blade from working. Mountain-Burden Stone also works, or any other custom magic or evocations people can come up with. Also the dagger isn't &amp;quot;crappy&amp;quot; unless compared to evocation investment. Loss of a speciality &amp; +1 attack/+3 dmg on withering attacks is not huge and may be the preferred option compared to the difficulty of retrieving your weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Im not an Anathema&quot; stealth option you mention about not using your daiklave tends to fall apart as soon as life or death is on the line (and still doesn't prevent the issue of Melee:Swords). <br /> <br /> I don't know any player who to have ever given up their artifact weapon to use a mundane weapon with a slight tactical advantage a la &quot;fighting a Crane stylist&quot; example. If they were gonna prep that far in advance PCs almost always choose some kind of ambush. Assuming they even have that information in the first place. <i>and that still doesn't make Melee:Swords less valid</i> because they probably don't have the specialty for Melee:Niche Combat Application. <br /> <br /> And last, Disarm was a red herring I wanted to avoid. I knew someone would suggest disarming as a way of neutralizing Melee Specialties but it ignores almost all melee specialties equally, so its a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T21:36:09-07:00","id":1222822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222819#post1222819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Crusader's specialty is specifically people in a Martial Arts Form Charm. I refer to those as stances a lot, I forgot to use the proper term.<br /> <br /> Afaik there isn't a game term for &quot;Mini Kaiju&quot; like DnD has for size catagories. Large Beasts (or Legendary Size Monsters) seems to broad to you, but do you actually veto the rules-sanctioned Melee: Swords at your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>First I have to go by what you say on this, I don't know what the specialty actually is so when you said the specialties were, &quot;people in a stance&quot; and &quot;big creatures&quot; considering your complaining I had to kind of assume that those were the actual wording on the specialties. As opposed to what you've just clarified them to, which make a lot of sense for their characters. If your character is dedicated towards a specific task why wouldn't you be able to apply the specialty they got for that task to the task they've trained for. <br /> <br /> As for vetoing the stuff that was too broad yes, I vetoed world history for our scientist when he wanted to us it for lore. Our night caste has warboomerangs as his thrown specialty because I don't see it as a problem. If it's not an artifact it can be removed from play by just destroying the bloody thing, if it is an artifact making sure a disarment leaves it at more than short distance from them, call the blade doesn't work outside of short range, prevents them from willing it back to their hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T22:04:04-07:00","id":1222827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222821#post1222821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;Im not an Anathema&quot; stealth option you mention about not using your daiklave tends to fall apart as soon as life or death is on the line (and still doesn't prevent the issue of Melee:Swords).<br /> <br /> I don't know any player who to have ever given up their artifact weapon to use a mundane weapon with a slight tactical advantage a la &quot;fighting a Crane stylist&quot; example. If they were gonna prep that far in advance PCs almost always choose some kind of ambush. Assuming they even have that information in the first place. <i>and that still doesn't make Melee:Swords less valid</i> because they probably don't have the specialty for Melee:Niche Combat Application.<br /> <br /> And last, Disarm was a red herring I wanted to avoid. I knew someone would suggest disarming as a way of neutralizing Melee Specialties but it ignores almost all melee specialties equally, so its a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every combat encounter has to be about life or death. They can still be an intense encounter where you still want to avoid using an artifact. Also it could cause issues with melee: swords as per what I have said about desirable tags for the situation. What if you did not want to deal lethal damage?<br /> <br /> Ignoring the +2 defence bonus from the full defence action on a decisive attack due to a weapon with the flexible tag is far more beneficial than the minor stat bonuses from an artifact that only apply to withering attacks, at least until evocations are applicable. Also you are assuming planning an ambush is possible and that its not a circumstance of a general threat around, such as aggressive nomads in the area who always ride on horse back, sure you could track them down and ambush them, but that would take time and is a distraction from whatever the circle is attempting to do. Also again with the exaggeration of either Melee: &quot;Weapon of Choice&quot; in comparison to &quot;Niche Combat Application&quot; with the implication that anything not a speciality in a weapon is so Niche its not worth taking. Specialities such as &quot;Researched Opponents&quot; , &quot;When outnumbered&quot; or &quot;Fighting cooperatively with a specific partner&quot; can all be interesting and frequently applicable. <br /> <br /> In regards to Disarm you already suggested that if a character was so invested in a particular artifact with a speciality relevant to it that they would specifically try get it back ignoring other melee weapon options. I highlighted that there are abilities out there that may deny that option and force them to improvise, which may result in going outside of their speciality if it is weapon or weapon type specific. If a speciality is tied to situation instead then it would still be applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T22:48:21-07:00","id":1222830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222821#post1222821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;Im not an Anathema&quot; stealth option you mention about not using your daiklave tends to fall apart as soon as life or death is on the line (and still doesn't prevent the issue of Melee:Swords).<br /> <br /> I don't know any player who to have ever given up their artifact weapon to use a mundane weapon with a slight tactical advantage a la &quot;fighting a Crane stylist&quot; example. If they were gonna prep that far in advance PCs almost always choose some kind of ambush. Assuming they even have that information in the first place. <i>and that still doesn't make Melee:Swords less valid</i> because they probably don't have the specialty for Melee:Niche Combat Application.<br /> <br /> And last, Disarm was a red herring I wanted to avoid. I knew someone would suggest disarming as a way of neutralizing Melee Specialties but it ignores almost all melee specialties equally, so its a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually the scientist in my group is constantly dealing with the debate on whether or not he wants to use his power bow or his crossbow. The crossbow fits his specialty as a thing he made and is thus more accurate and such, but it doesn't hit as hard as the powerbow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T00:44:10-07:00","id":1222844,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Specialties are bad.<br /> <br /> They never result in interesting gameplay at my table. We've been playing since 1st Edition and I cannot remember once that a PC stewed over a decision for the sake of a specialty.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, they exist to give the PCs a bonus die and defense boost, something that would be better accomplished with stunt rules.<br /> <br /> Edit, days later: I suppose it also interjects some personality into long stat blocks for NPC write-ups. A better solution: don't bore the reader with long stat blocks. 3rd Edition wisely did away with those, for the most part. It's time for specialties to follow! Another sacrifice for the hecatomb!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","user":"Ketrus","date":". 06-02-2018, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T01:07:11-07:00","id":1222846,"title":"","content":"Like the idea of Specialties, as in something which distinguishes a character, but the fact that they are equally expensive and cover hugely varying areas of applicability means incentives to game them are strong... Less so without the 3 limit in 3e, but nonetheless. Would be more fun with a finite list of them which are reasonably &quot;balanced&quot; and for mortals, seem a bit unnecessary for Exalted (where Charms cover characters ability to be better in some situations than others)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T04:26:38-07:00","id":1222860,"title":"","content":"What about stuff like the sword user finding an artifact 5 goremaul or something? <br /> <br /> That said, I like the idea of splitting specialities into broad/narrow/niche. It does raise questions like what tier a speciality for a specific daiklave a player always carries would be though. <br /> <br /> Cos like, technically a speciality for a single sword is <i>super specific</i> but they'd get it all the time unless you had somebody nick it or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T05:37:50-07:00","id":1222865,"title":"","content":"In part that complication on determining the broadness/applicability is <i>why</i> it can be that broad.<br /> <br /> Starting from &quot;we don't want to fudge the math&quot;, I'm fine treating specialties as flaws to give xp, and finding a threshold where that applies.<br /> And as for something like Melee(Swords)... well, I see no point in complaining that a player that went out of his way to make sure he has a sword in hand... will usually have the sword in hand whenever he wants. That XP spent on call the blade, summon the loyal steel and glorious solar saber could well have seen better use somewhere else. Gods know there's never enough XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 05-29-2018, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:03:23-07:00","id":1222873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222860#post1222860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about stuff like the sword user finding an artifact 5 goremaul or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the main circumstance I see it come up. Someone has &quot;specialty: long sword&quot; with their steel sword, and then they find a grimcleaver or something. I was tempted to take a specialty in Short Swords, but as I found twin goremauls, I'm glad I didn't.<br /> (As specialties are only 3xp of course, it doesn't make a huge difference, you just buy a new specialty.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead, I took a Melee specialty of &quot;2 weapon fighting.&quot; You'd think it'd apply all the time, right? After all, I carry two swords, and have Call the Blade if I get disarmed.<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't apply now, because an Essence 5 Dawn Caste cut off my hand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-29-2018, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:12:39-07:00","id":1222876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222873#post1222873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the main circumstance I see it come up. Someone has &quot;specialty: long sword&quot; with their steel sword, and then they find a grimcleaver or something. I was tempted to take a specialty in Short Swords, but as I found twin goremauls, I'm glad I didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead, I took a Melee specialty of &quot;2 weapon fighting.&quot; You'd think it'd apply all the time, right? After all, I carry two swords, and have Call the Blade if I get disarmed.<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't apply now, because an Essence 5 Dawn Caste cut off my hand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Get a hook!! Or maybe a scimitar replacement. That'l show that pesky dawn!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:13:29-07:00","id":1222877,"title":"","content":"I mean, the way I see it if a player is going out of their way to ensure that a speciality always applies, that means it's still affecting the game in a way that an extra dot of the ability wouldn't. <br /> <br /> And really, is it so bad that in practice a speciality just means that your dice pool goes up to 11?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:32:01-07:00","id":1222881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1222876#post1222876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get a hook!! Or maybe a scimitar replacement. That'l show that pesky dawn!</div> </div> </div> </div>I crafted myself a fake hand, so when I was dragged before the area's Solar Queen and put on trial for murder, with several Solar witnesses saying it was me, I could wave my fake hand in the air and insist that I can't be the murderer. It worked too. Craft turns out to be pretty useful for a Night Caste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And really, is it so bad that in practice a speciality just means that your dice pool goes up to 11? </div> </div> </div>TBH, I generally assume the game expects your specialties to come up a lot, considering how wide many of the examples are, and that's why they've been cut from +3 max to +1 max.<br /> <br /> Back in 2nd ed, I often saw Dragonblood with Dodge 5 (+3 armoured) or Dodge 5 (+3 unarmoured).<br /> <br /> <br /> I mostly use specialties as a kind of flavour. My character is from the North, so he has Survival (North+1). Right now, he's in a desert, so it's not much use, but if we were in the North it'd come up all the time. But I just think it makes sense that he's better at surviving snow-covered tundra than sandy deserts.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if your guy is a famous swordsman I think it's fine that he has Melee (+1 swords). If he fights with a sword constantly, I'd expect him to be better with swords than with whips or tetsubos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:49:48-07:00","id":1222883,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't mind Specialties coming up most of the time, its cool to be creative with them, but I don't mind being lazy/laid back either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-29-2018, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T12:30:14-07:00","id":1222966,"title":"","content":"Two solutions I've used in the past are:<br /> <br /> 1)Specialties cannot be so broad as to apply to every situation, and specialties must be a descriptive phrasing using 2 or more words.<br /> <br /> 2)Specialties are your 5th dot. Skills go to 4 dots and to get access to the 5th, you can only do so while using the specialty. Usually in combination with rule 1. Reason for this is to head off some common complaints and problems from maxing-out assumptions making scaling challenges really dumb if everyone is just maxed out all the time.<br /> <br /> If I were to go with a streamlined solution, I'd just nix them altogether. You don't lose much if everyone is functionally losing a die they get almost all the time anyhow. Do they really value-add in mental or storytelling consideration or is it just another avenue for optimization? My experience is without houserules, it's almost always the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:17:28-07:00","id":1223005,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind is that if you completely nix Specialities, or make them the fifth dot, is that now can mess with Dragon-Blooded a fair bit. Sure, it's just one more die or one more Defense to a Solar, but to a DB, it is one more die, one more Defense, one more Charm die, and potentially one more automatic Charm success or Charm Defense.<br /> <br /> Now making them slightly more restrictive I can understand (and I kinda like that they must be a descriptive phrase with 2 or more words), but it is important to note that they are no longer &quot;just&quot; one more die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:28:41-07:00","id":1223010,"title":"","content":"Two dice difference for DB in point of fact:. 6+6 vs 5+5 with full excellency","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T15:13:30-07:00","id":1223031,"title":"","content":"Yeah, removing specialities entirely shoots dragonblooded in the balls. Especially in 3e where some of their excellencies work off successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T15:28:06-07:00","id":1223038,"title":"","content":"Not to mention there\u2019s a good chunk of DB charms that actually add excellencies ad hoc. In fact those kind of charms kind of encourage you to have more flavourful excellencies rather than broad ones, because you can pick up ones that you need if and when you need them, and treat your character sheet specialties as benefits that you get when operating in your field of expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T17:37:10-07:00","id":1223073,"title":"","content":"I remain unconvinced that <i>I</i> should hate Melee specialties, but please feel free to continue your dislike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T01:16:20-07:00","id":1223135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not every combat encounter has to be about life or death. They can still be an intense encounter where you still want to avoid using an artifact. Also it could cause issues with melee: swords as per what I have said about desirable tags for the situation. What if you did not want to deal lethal damage? </div> </div> </div>A stunt where they hit them with the flat of the blade? Or carry around some Kenshin style reverse blade sword for when you just want to bludgeon people into submission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T01:54:39-07:00","id":1223137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223135#post1223135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A stunt where they hit them with the flat of the blade? Or carry around some Kenshin style reverse blade sword for when you just want to bludgeon people into submission.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using a weapon in a way its not designed for? Sounds like a circumstance that reasonable ST should be applying a penalty and or the improvised tag. Stunt or no Stunt. Now if your specifically carrying a weapon around to handle this kind of situation that suits your speciality, great! That's an excellent way of being prepared and planning in advance to stay within your speciality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T04:44:56-07:00","id":1223163,"title":"","content":"You don't apply penalties due to stuff done as a stunt. That defeats the point of a stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:45:00-07:00","id":1223272,"title":"","content":"I'm 80% sure that the book says somewhere specifically that you can deal bashing damage with a stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T11:49:27-07:00","id":1223342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223163#post1223163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't apply penalties due to stuff done as a stunt. That defeats the point of a stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you back that up please? Looking at the rules stunts say nothing of ignoring penalties. <br /> <br /> Edit: The penalty isnt applied because the action is a stunt. The penalty is applied because you are using a weapon to do something its not designed to do. Stunting certainly helps with describing how and provides its bonus still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","user":"Klaek","date":". 05-30-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:51:06-07:00","id":1223361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223342#post1223342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you back that up please? Looking at the rules stunts say nothing of ignoring penalties.<br /> <br /> Edit: The penalty isnt applied because the action is a stunt. The penalty is applied because you are using a weapon to do something its not designed to do. Stunting certainly helps with describing how and provides its bonus still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapon tags<br /> <br /> &quot;Lethal: This weapon normally does lethal damage when<br /> used to deliver a decisive attack. Lethal close combat<br /> weapons can deliver bashing damage with an appropriate<br /> stunt, by e.g. attacking with the pommel or with the flat<br /> of the blade.&quot;<br /> <br /> The intent of the rules is pretty clear. Dealing bashing with a lethal tag weapon is a matter of stunting, not applying penalties. It is a function of the weapon.<br /> <br /> You are probably not very familiar with fighting techniques or weapon design in general, hitting with the side of the blade, with the pommel, with a shaft are all very much what a weapon is designed for and fighters train to do this. It is part of holistically using your weapon.<br /> <br /> You should not face a penalty for butting someone with your spear shaft instead of sticking the pointy end on them. The spear is designed for both, and a properly trained fighter can do both as easily and as effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-30-2018, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:07:29-07:00","id":1223366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223361#post1223361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weapon tags<br /> <br /> &quot;Lethal: This weapon normally does lethal damage when<br /> used to deliver a decisive attack. Lethal close combat<br /> weapons can deliver bashing damage with an appropriate<br /> stunt, by e.g. attacking with the pommel or with the flat<br /> of the blade.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, not sure how i missed that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:10:01-07:00","id":1223368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223361#post1223361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are probably not very familiar with fighting techniques or weapon design in general, hitting with the side of the blade, with the pommel, with a shaft are all very much what a weapon is designed for and fighters train to do this. It is part of holistically using your weapon.<br /> <br /> You should not face a penalty for butting someone with your spear shaft instead of sticking the pointy end on them. The spear is designed for both, and a properly trained fighter can do both as easily and as effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and in 99% of cases you're right, but I might require a really big stunt, or apply a penalty, to do bashing with a shuriken or a rapier maybe. Either way if you're a Solar you likely have the dice to destroy a defense even with a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:24:58-07:00","id":1223375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223368#post1223368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, and in 99% of cases you're right, but I might require a really big stunt, or apply a penalty, to do bashing with a shuriken or a rapier maybe. Either way if you're a Solar you likely have the dice to destroy a defense even with a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are some edge cases that will push the limits a bit, a rapier still has a guard and pommel, though a pointy star shuriken, as opposed to a design that has a blunt end, would be pretty difficult to stunt.<br /> <br /> Like in most cases, shits gotta make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:15:30-07:00","id":1223394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too?p=1223366#post1223366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, not sure how i missed that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:29:45-07:00","id":1223400,"title":"","content":"Concept: Split Melee into topics like Lore, and allow Specialties orthogonal to that. Axes and spears and swords seem different enough to me that using them all with Melee never made too much sense. Of course there's still a Charm to let you cross-apply, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:56:59-07:00","id":1223414,"title":"","content":"Eh, at that point you start saying &quot;aren't sailing a boat and an airship very different? Aren't running and lifting quite different? Aren't trading and filling out paperwork quite different? Aren't playing an instrument and acting quite different?&quot; Which they, to some extent, are, but you'd end up with far too many abilities.<br /> I'd say spears and swords are different enough for specialities, not for whole abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T03:32:58-07:00","id":1223564,"title":"","content":"Differentiating weapons is what martial arts are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}